The seat is currently held by [[James Gallagher (California politician)|James Gallagher]], who won a special election to finish the term of Republican [[Doug LaMalfa]],<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.politico.com/news/2026/01/06/doug-lamalfa-dead-00712222 |title=GOP Lawmaker Doug Lamalfa dies at 65 |author=Meredith Lee Hill |work=Politico |date=January 6, 2026 |access-date=January 6, 2026}}</ref> who was re-elected with 65.3% of the vote in 2024.<ref name="HPVT"/> A [[2026 California's 1st congressional district special election|special election]] using the electoral boundaries pre-[[2025 California Proposition 50|Proposition 50]] was held on June 2, 2026.

