===Primary===
====Campaign====
In the June 2026 [[Nonpartisan blanket primary|top-two primary]], the principal Democratic candidates were Villegas and [[Jasmeet Bains]], a physician and member of the [[California State Assembly]].<ref name=KQED2026TossUp>{{cite news |last1=Lagos |first1=Marisa |last2=Shafer |first2=Scott |last3=Marzorati |first3=Guy |title=Two Democrats Are Fighting for the Chance to Flip California’s Only Toss-Up House Race |url=https://www.kqed.org/news/12085418/two-democrats-are-fighting-for-the-chance-to-flip-californias-only-toss-up-house-race |work=KQED |date=May 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260528234357/https://www.kqed.org/news/12085418/two-democrats-are-fighting-for-the-chance-to-flip-californias-only-toss-up-house-race |archive-date=May 28, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Bains was endorsed by numerous state party officials<ref name="CalMattersPrimary">{{cite news |last=Miller |first=Maya C. |title=Villegas defeats Bains in Central Valley House race |url=https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/06/22nd-district-primary-villegas/ |work=[[CalMatters]] |date=June 9, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260610173917/https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/06/22nd-district-primary-villegas/ |archive-date=June 10, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="APGeneral">{{cite news |last=Cooper |first=Jonathan J. |title=US House race in California will test progressives' appeal in GOP district |url=https://apnews.com/article/randy-villegas-house-seat-david-valadao-democrats-2c1d1c69ccbcc47c3c53b6297c21f40b |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260611184150/https://apnews.com/article/randy-villegas-house-seat-david-valadao-democrats-2c1d1c69ccbcc47c3c53b6297c21f40b |archive-date=June 11, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> and the [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]] (DCCC),<ref name="APGeneral" /><ref name=NYTimes2026Advances /> an unusual intervention by the national party in a contested primary.<ref>{{cite news |last=Miller |first=Maya C. |title=National Democrats said they'd stay out of this California race. Then they picked a side |url=https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/05/central-valley-congress-dccc/ |work=CalMatters |date=May 21, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260521233546/https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/05/central-valley-congress-dccc/ |archive-date=May 21, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Koseff |first=Alexei |title=This California district is a must-win for Democrats. They're fighting over who can flip it |url=https://www.sfchronicle.com/politics/article/jasmeet-bains-randy-villegas-david-valadao-22261629.php/ |newspaper=San Francisco Chronicle |date=May 20, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260521114236/https://www.sfchronicle.com/politics/article/jasmeet-bains-randy-villegas-david-valadao-22261629.php |archive-date=May 21, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The DCCC's endorsement caused severe disagreement within the Democratic Party.<ref>{{cite news |last=Nixon |first=Nicole |title=A bitter slugfest in Central Valley exposes divisions in the Democratic Party |url=https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-05-28/bitter-slugfest-in-central-valley-exposes-divisions-in-democratic-party |newspaper=Los Angeles Times |date=May 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260528105318/https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-05-28/bitter-slugfest-in-central-valley-exposes-divisions-in-democratic-party |archive-date=May 28, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=Prospect2026Planned>{{cite news |last=Janssen |first=Emma |title=Planned Parenthood Puts Its Thumb on the Scale in California |url=https://prospect.org/2026/05/15/planned-parenthood-congressional-primary-california-bains-valadao-villegas/ |work=The American Prospect |date=May 15, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260515110146/https://prospect.org/2026/05/15/planned-parenthood-congressional-primary-california-bains-valadao-villegas/ |archive-date=May 15, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=Prospect2026Moderation>{{cite news |last=Janssen |first=Emma |title=Establishment Dems and the Self-Fulfilling Prophecy of Moderation |url=https://prospect.org/2026/05/06/establishment-dems-self-fulfilling-prophecy-of-moderation/ |work=The American Prospect |date=May 6, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260506092204/https://prospect.org/2026/05/06/establishment-dems-self-fulfilling-prophecy-of-moderation/ |archive-date=May 6, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Progressive Democrats criticized the DCCC's intervention and said "voters should pick nominees", including [[Pramila Jayapal]], [[Greg Casar]], and [[Maxwell Frost]],<ref>{{cite news |last=Solender |first=Andrew |title=Scoop: House Dems issue rare rebuke of their own campaign arm |url=https://www.axios.com/2026/05/04/democrats-primary-california-bains-villegas-dccc |work=Axios |date=May 4, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-date=May 5, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260505042505/https://www.axios.com/2026/05/04/democrats-primary-california-bains-villegas-dccc}}</ref> while the DCCC argued that Bains was well positioned to defeat Valadao in the general election.<ref name="APGeneral" /><ref>{{cite news |last=Johnson |first=Jake |title=Dem Establishment Accused of ‘Putting Thumb on the Scale’ Against Progressive Candidate |url=https://www.commondreams.org/news/randy-villegas-dccc |work=Common Dreams |date=May 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260504144628/https://www.commondreams.org/news/randy-villegas-dccc |archive-date=May 4, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> The primary was often framed as a battle between the party's "establishment" and "progressive" wing.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gómez |first1=Fin Daniel |last2=Hubbard |first2=Kaia |title=Primary fight in key California Latino district highlights questions over Democratic Party's future |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/primary-fight-california-latino-district-democratic-party-bains-villegas-valadeo/ |work=CBS News |date=May 22, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260522164904/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/primary-fight-california-latino-district-democratic-party-bains-villegas-valadeo/ |archive-date=May 22, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Yilek |first=Caitlin |title=GOP Rep. Valadao to face progressive Villegas in key California House district, in defeat for moderate Democrats |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/gop-rep-valadao-progressive-villegas-california-house-district/ |work=CBS News |date=June 9, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260610070144/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/gop-rep-valadao-progressive-villegas-california-house-district/ |archive-date=June 10, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Klein |first=Kerry |title='A tug of war for the identity of the party'—why a Valley congressional race is key for Democrats |url=https://www.kvpr.org/local-news/2026-05-27/a-tug-of-war-for-the-identity-of-the-party-why-a-valley-congressional-race-is-key-for-democrats |work=KVPR |date=May 27, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260529024017/https://www.kvpr.org/local-news/2026-05-27/a-tug-of-war-for-the-identity-of-the-party-why-a-valley-congressional-race-is-key-for-democrats |archive-date=May 29, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Alvarado |first=Isaías |title=Una disputa entre demócratas se cierne sobre la elección de un distrito congresional hispano en California |url=https://elpais.com/us/2026-06-01/una-disputa-entre-democratas-se-cierne-sobre-la-eleccion-de-un-distrito-congresional-hispano-en-california.html |language=es |newspaper=El País |date=June 1, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260602065026/https://elpais.com/us/2026-06-01/una-disputa-entre-democratas-se-cierne-sobre-la-eleccion-de-un-distrito-congresional-hispano-en-california.html |archive-date=June 2, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Outside groups spent more than $2.2 million on advertising against Villegas during the final month of the primary, including organizations associated with centrist Democrats, the Republican Party.<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /> The pro-Israel organization [[Democratic Majority for Israel]] alone spent over $500,000 against Villegas.<ref>{{cite news |last=Gligich |first=Daniel |title=Pro-Israel launches ad blitz against Villegas in Dem primary against Valadao |url=https://sjvsun.com/news/politics/pro-israel-launches-ad-blitz-against-villegas-in-dem-primary-against-valadao/ |work=The San Joaquin Valley Sun |date=May 10, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260510183048/https://sjvsun.com/news/politics/pro-israel-launches-ad-blitz-against-villegas-in-dem-primary-against-valadao/ |archive-date=May 10, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Goldstein |first=Luke |title=The Israel Lobby Is Picking Sides in a California Primary |url=https://jacobin.com/2026/05/israel-democrats-money-california-primary |work=Jacobin |date=May 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260911081725/https://jacobin.com/2026/05/israel-democrats-money-california-primary |archive-date=September 11, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Villegas campaigned as a progressive and left-wing economic populist,<ref>{{cite news |last=Sosa |first=Anabel |title=Progressive endorsed by Bernie Sanders moves forward in Central Valley swing district |url=https://www.sfgate.com/politics/article/california-house-race-central-valley-22299569.php |work=SFGate |date=June 10, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260913130311/https://www.sfgate.com/politics/article/california-house-race-central-valley-22299569.php |archive-date=September 13, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=Prospect2026Majority>{{cite news |last=Dayen |first=David |title=The New Majority Makers |url=https://prospect.org/2026/09/14/oct-2026-the-new-majority-makers/ |work=The American Prospect |date=September 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260914104709/https://prospect.org/2026/09/14/oct-2026-the-new-majority-makers/ |archive-date=September 14, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> with the [[Associated Press]] calling him a "populist insurgent".<ref name="APGeneral" /> His campaign emphasized the cost of living, health care, labor rights, public education, immigration reform, and opposition to corporate influence in politics.<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /><ref name="APGeneral" /> Villegas was endorsed by [[Bernie Sanders]],<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /><ref name=NBC2026Wading>{{cite news |last=Smith |first=Allan |title=Bernie Sanders endorses Randy Villegas, wading into a Democratic fight in a key House battleground |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/bernie-sanders-endorses-randy-villegas-wading-democratic-fight-key-hou-rcna244291 |work=NBC News |date=November 17, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260323065659/https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/bernie-sanders-endorses-randy-villegas-wading-democratic-fight-key-hou-rcna244291 |archive-date=March 23, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez]],<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /> [[Dolores Huerta]],<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /> [[Ro Khanna]],<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /><ref>{{cite news |last=Blood |first=Michael R. |title=After years of defying the odds, California's David Valadao faces new test as Latinos turn on Trump |url=https://www.aol.com/articles/years-defying-odds-californias-david-130238000.html |agency=Associated Press |work=AOL |date=September 5, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260912065633/https://www.aol.com/articles/years-defying-odds-californias-david-130238000.html |archive-date=September 12, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> the [[Congressional Progressive Caucus]],<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /> and the [[California Working Families Party]].<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /> Despite the DCCC's support for Bains, Villegas secured a key endorsement from the [[Congressional Hispanic Caucus]].<ref name="NYTPrimaryEndorsements">{{cite news |last=Edmondson |first=Catie |title=House Democrats’ Primary Endorsements Divide the Party |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/06/us/politics/house-democrats-primary-endorsements.html |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=May 6, 2026}}</ref>

In the June primary results, Valadao finished first with 40.7%, Villegas second with 32.4%, and Bains third with 26.9%. Valadao and Villegas advanced to the general election.<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /><ref name="APGeneral" /> Villegas' win against Bain was a major "anti-establishment" upset,<ref name="APGeneral" /><ref name=NYTimes2026Advances>{{cite news |last1=Browning |first1=Kellen |title=Sanders-Backed Progressive Advances in California Swing District Against Valadao |work=New York Times |date=June 9, 2026 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/09/us/politics/bains-villegas-california-democrats-primary.html}}</ref><ref name=WashingtonPost2026Liberal>{{cite news |title=Liberal advances to California general election, dealing a blow to establishment Democrats |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/06/10/randy-villegas-secures-spot-run-off-key-california-house-race/ |newspaper=The Washington Post |date=June 9, 2026 |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20261003042907/https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2026/06/10/randy-villegas-secures-spot-run-off-key-california-house-race/ |archive-date=October 3, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> which ''[[CalMatters]]'' described as a "stunning rebuke of establishment politics"<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /> After the primary, Democratic elected officials who had supported Bains endorsed Villegas for the general election.<ref name="CalMattersPrimary" /><ref name="APGeneral" /> In June, some progresive members of Congress threatened to withhold their dues from the DCCC unless it changed course.<ref>{{cite news |last=Solender |first=Andrew |title=Dems threaten to withhold DCCC dues over California faceplant |url=https://www.axios.com/2026/06/09/democrats-house-primary-california-villegas-bains |work=Axios |date=June 9, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-date=June 9, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260609211930/https://www.axios.com/2026/06/09/democrats-house-primary-california-villegas-bains}}</ref> In September, the DCCC endorsed Villegas.<ref>{{cite news |last=Parsley |first=Haley |title=DCCC backs progressive Randy Villegas for Congress following Bains’ defeat |url=https://www.sacbee.com/news/politics-government/capitol-alert/article316082675.html |newspaper=The Sacramento Bee |date=June 12, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261003030619/https://www.sacbee.com/news/politics-government/capitol-alert/article316082675.html |archive-date=October 3, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Villegas is a rare outspoken progressives in a competitive swing seat,<ref name=Prospect2026Majority /> and hopes to energize working-class voters with a progressive, economic populist agenda.<ref name=Bloomberg2026Reframe>{{cite news |last=Sheehey |first=Maeve |title=California’s New House Map Reframes the Fight for GOP Incumbents |url=https://news.bloomberglaw.com/bloomberg-government-news/californias-new-house-map-reframes-the-fight-for-gop-incumbents |work=Bloomberg Government |date=August 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20261003025025/https://news.bloomberglaw.com/bloomberg-government-news/californias-new-house-map-reframes-the-fight-for-gop-incumbents |archive-date=October 3, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=Prospect2026Valley>{{cite news |last=Janssen |first=Emma |title=How Do You Beat a Central Valley Republican? |url=https://prospect.org/2026/04/28/how-do-you-beat-central-valley-republican-california-congress-valadao-bains-villegas/ |work=The American Prospect |date=April 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260428093332/https://prospect.org/2026/04/28/how-do-you-beat-central-valley-republican-california-congress-valadao-bains-villegas/ |archive-date=April 28, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=McDaniel |first=Justine |title=Will the economy motivate voters? This Central Valley swing district could be a test |url=https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2026-09-13/will-economy-motivate-voters-this-central-valley-swing-district-could-be-test |newspaper=Los Angeles Times |date=September 13, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260923081520/https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2026-09-13/will-economy-motivate-voters-this-central-valley-swing-district-could-be-test |archive-date=September 23, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> In September, [[Bernie Sanders]] campaigned for Villegas.<ref>{{cite news |last=Miranda |first=Mathew |title=Mike Johnson, Bernie Sanders to campaign in Central Valley for 22nd District race |url=https://www.arcamax.com/politics/politicalnews/s-4308789 |work=The Sacramento Bee |via=ArcaMax |date=September 29, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261001064507/https://www.arcamax.com/politics/politicalnews/s-4308789 |archive-date=October 1, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

