===General election===
====Campaign====
Although Gomez is part of the [[Congressional Progressive Caucus]], his acceptance of funding from the [[cryptocurrency]] industry and from [[American Israel Public Affairs Committee]] (AIPAC) led most progressive organizations to instead endorse Gonzales-Torres in the primary and general,<ref name=Salon2025Target>{{cite news |title=Progressive Dems pick their latest primary target — and it's a modest surprise |newspaper=[[Salon.com|Salon]] |first=Russell |last=Payne |date=September 5, 2025 |url=https://www.salon.com/2025/09/05/progressive-dems-pick-their-latest-primary-target-and-its-a-modest-surprise/}}</ref><ref name="Intercept-endorsement">{{cite news |title=Will AIPAC Save Jimmy Gomez Again? / She's Challenging an AIPAC Democrat. A National Progressive Group Wants In. |first=Akela |last=Lacy |work=The Intercept |date=September 4, 2025 |url=https://theintercept.com/2025/09/04/aipac-la-jimmy-gomez-primary-gonzales-torres/}}</ref><ref name="LAT-endorsement">{{cite news |title=Influential group behind Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez's victory seeks to oust L.A. Democratic congressman |first=Julia |last=Wick |work=Los Angeles Times |via=AOL |date=September 4, 2025 |url=https://www.aol.com/news/influential-left-wing-group-seeks-124500345.html}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Wu |first=Nicholas |title=California Dem faces election turbulence |url=https://www.semafor.com/article/09/10/2026/california-dem-faces-election-turbulence |website=Semafor |date=11 September 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260911173354/https://www.semafor.com/article/09/10/2026/california-dem-faces-election-turbulence |archive-date=11 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Weigel |first=David |title=Democratic primary challengers see an opening on Israel |url=https://www.semafor.com/article/10/06/2025/democratic-primary-challengers-see-an-opening-on-israel |work=Semafor |date=October 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260907172724/https://www.semafor.com/article/10/06/2025/democratic-primary-challengers-see-an-opening-on-israel |archive-date=September 7, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> including the [[Justice Democrats]],<ref name="Intercept-endorsement"/><ref name="LAT-endorsement" /> [[Our Revolution]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Angela Gonzales-Torres for Congress (CA-34) |url=https://ourrevolution.com/angela-gonzales-torres-for-congress-ca-34/ |publisher=Our Revolution |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927015806/https://ourrevolution.com/angela-gonzales-torres-for-congress-ca-34/ |archive-date=September 27, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> the [[Working Families Party|California Working Families Party]]<ref>{{cite web |title=We're proud to endorse Angela Gonzales-Torres for Congress |website=Facebook |publisher=California Working Families Party |url=https://www.facebook.com/CAWFP/posts/were-proud-to-endorse-angela-gonzales-torres-for-congress-working-families-in-ca/1240628124836852/}}</ref> and [[Los Angeles Democratic Socialists of America]].<ref name=ShakeUpLA2026General>{{cite web |publisher=Los Angeles Democatic Socialists of America |title=Meet Our Candidates! |url=https://shakeup-la.com/our-candidates |url-status=live |archive-date=September 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260904180506/https://shakeup-la.com/our-candidates |quote=The Los Angeles chapter of the Democratic Socialists of America (DSA-LA) is proud to endorse nine our fellow members for the 2026 general election.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Goldberg |first=Noah |title=Democratic Socialists endorse Raman in L.A. mayoral race |url=https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-09-02/democratic-socialists-endorse-raman-in-la-mayoral-race |work=Los Angeles Times |date=September 2, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260903190739/https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2026-09-02/democratic-socialists-endorse-raman-in-la-mayoral-race |archive-date=September 3, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author=DSA members across California |title=Democratic Socialism in the 2026 California Elections: Local Chapter Reports |url=https://www.californiadsa.org/news/0we87mn67kqp7xb7dy9tlp9x3wkhd0 |publisher=California DSA |date=September 22, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260926045337/https://www.californiadsa.org/news/0we87mn67kqp7xb7dy9tlp9x3wkhd0 |archive-date=September 26, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

In August, the [[United States House Committee on Ethics|House Ethics Committee]] began an inquiry into whether Gomez had engaged in sexual misconduct.<ref>{{cite news |title=House Ethics Committee announces sexual misconduct investigation into Rep. Jimmy Gomez |work=Los Angeles Times |via=Yahoo News |date=August 2026 |first=Ben |last=Wieder |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/politics/articles/house-ethics-committee-announces-sexual-222331271.html}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=House Ethics Committee unveils sexual misconduct probe into Representative Jimmy Gomez |work=Courthouse News Service |date=August 2026 |first=Benjamin |last=Weiss |url=https://www.courthousenews.com/house-ethics-committee-unveils-sexual-misconduct-probe-into-representative-jimmy-gomez/}}</ref><ref name="Downballot">{{cite news |title=Morning Digest: Ethics Committee investigation roils Democrat vs. Democrat general election |first=Jeff |last=Singer |work=The Downballot |date=August 2026 |url=https://www.the-downballot.com/p/morning-digest-ethics-committee-investigation}}</ref> The inquiry followed one into [[Eric Swalwell]], with whom Gomez was personal friends and who had appointed Gomez chair of his [[2026 California gubernatorial election|Swalwell's gubernatorial campaign]] before Swalwell suspended the campaign and resigned from Congress amid criminal investigations into alleged rape and sexual misconduct.<ref name=AP2026Swalwell>{{Cite web |last=Press |first=Associated |date=2026-04-11 |title=Allies yank support for Swalwell's California governor run after sexual assault allegations |url=https://www.courthousenews.com/allies-yank-support-for-swalwells-california-governor-run-after-sexual-assault-allegations |access-date=2026-08-16 |website=Courthouse News Service |language=en-us}}</ref><ref name=Politico2026Holden>{{Cite web |last=Holden |first=Lindsey |date=2026-07-16 |title=Israel and ethics dog Jimmy Gomez |url=https://www.politico.com/newsletters/california-playbook-pm/2026/07/16/gomez-investigation-israel-01001619 |access-date=2026-08-16 |website=POLITICO |language=en}}</ref><ref name=CalMatters2026Yu>{{Cite news |last=Yu |first=Jeanne Kuang, Yue Stella |date=2026-04-10 |title=Supporters flee Swalwell's governor campaign amid allegations of sexual assault |url=https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/04/california-governor-race-swalwell-allegations/ |access-date=2026-08-16 |work=CalMatters |language=en-US}}</ref> One former Gomez staffer accused him of sexual assault.<ref>{{cite news |title=Rep. Jimmy Gomez accuser told House Ethics Committee he sexually assaulted her, attorneys say |first1=Allison |last1=Gordon |first2=Pamela |last2=Brown |work=CNN |date=August 19, 2026 |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/08/19/politics/jimmy-gomez-house-ethics-sexual-assault-allegation-invs}}</ref> Gomez denied any nonconsensual conduct and said that he had made personal mistakes outside his marriage.<ref>{{cite news |last=Solender |first=Andrew |title=House Ethics investigating Rep. Jimmy Gomez over sexual misconduct allegations |work=Axios |date=August 17, 2026 |url=https://www.axios.com/2026/08/17/ethics-investigating-jimmy-gomez-sexual-misconduct}}</ref> Gonzales-Torres criticized a "culture in Congress in which men abuse women"<ref>{{cite news |first=Eric |last=McDaniel |title=Jimmy Gomez under investigation for alleged sexual misconduct |work=NPR |date=August 17, 2026 |url=https://www.npr.org/2026/08/17/nx-s1-5935513/jimmy-gomez-house-ethics-investigation}}</ref> and said Gomez should withdraw.<ref>{{cite news |title=Angela Gonzales-Torres Calls on Rep. Jimmy Gomez to Withdraw from Race |first=Kathleen |last=Craughwell |publisher=Eagle Pop Rock |url=https://www.eaglerockpop.com/p/jimmy-gomez-challenger-calls-on-him-to-withdraw-from-congressional-race |quote="Rep. Jimmy Gomez should withdraw from the CA-34 race," Gonzales-Torres told Eagle Rock Pop Thursday. "I'd point to his own standard. In April he resigned as chair of Eric Swalwell's campaign for governor and said Swalwell should leave the race so there could be full accountability. That's a standard he needs to apply to himself."}}</ref>

